          "Create comprehensive Orders API documentation",
          "# Orders API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Orders API provides a client interface for interacting with the order management endpoints, allowing applications to create, read, update, and delete orders within the PolygonExpress platform.\n\n## Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    OrdersApi[Orders API] --> ApiClient[API Client]\n    OrdersApi --> OrderModels[Order Models]\n    \n    ApiClient --> HttpClient[HTTP Client]\n    ApiClient --> AuthService[Auth Service]\n    \n    subgraph \"API Layer\"\n        OrdersApi\n        ApiClient\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Supporting Services\"\n        HttpClient\n        AuthService\n        OrderModels\n    end\n```\n\n## API Methods\n\n```typescript\nclass OrdersApi {\n  /**\n   * Fetch all orders for the current user\n   * @returns Promise<Order[]> List of orders\n   * @throws ApiError if request fails\n   */\n  async getOrders(): Promise<Order[]>;\n  \n  /**\n   * Fetch a specific order by ID\n   * @param orderId The unique order identifier\n   * @returns Promise<Order> The order details\n   * @throws ApiError if order not found or request fails\n   */\n  async getOrderById(orderId: string): Promise<Order>;\n  \n  /**\n   * Create a new order\n   * @param orderData The order creation request\n   * @returns Promise<Order> The created order\n   * @throws ApiError if creation fails or validation errors\n   */\n  async createOrder(orderData: CreateOrderRequest): Promise<Order>;\n  \n  /**\n   * Update an existing order\n   * @param orderId The unique order identifier\n   * @param orderData The order update request\n   * @returns Promise<Order> The updated order\n   * @throws ApiError if update fails or validation errors\n   */\n  async updateOrder(orderId: string, orderData: UpdateOrderRequest): Promise<Order>;\n  \n  /**\n   * Cancel an existing order\n   * @param orderId The unique order identifier\n   * @returns Promise<void>\n   * @throws ApiError if cancellation fails\n   */\n  async cancelOrder(orderId: string): Promise<void>;\n}\n```\n\n## Data Models\n\n```typescript\ninterface Order {\n  id: string;\n  userId: string;\n  status: OrderStatus;\n  items: OrderItem[];\n  total: number;\n  createdAt: string;\n  updatedAt: string;\n}\n\nenum OrderStatus {\n  PENDING = 'pending',\n  PROCESSING = 'processing',\n  COMPLETED = 'completed',\n  CANCELLED = 'cancelled'\n}\n\ninterface OrderItem {\n  id: string;\n  productId: string;\n  quantity: number;\n  price: number;\n}\n\ninterface CreateOrderRequest {\n  items: {\n    productId: string;\n    quantity: number;\n  }[];\n}\n\ninterface UpdateOrderRequest {\n  status?: OrderStatus;\n  items?: {\n    productId: string;\n    quantity: number;\n  }[];\n}\n```\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n```typescript\nimport { ordersApi } from '@/api';\n\n// Fetch all orders\nconst fetchOrders = async () => {\n  try {\n    const orders = await ordersApi.getOrders();\n    return orders;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to fetch orders:', error);\n    throw error;\n  }\n};\n\n// Create a new order\nconst createOrder = async (items) => {\n  try {\n    const newOrder = await ordersApi.createOrder({ items });\n    return newOrder;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to create order:', error);\n    throw error;\n  }\n};\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\nThe Orders API handles errors using a standardized pattern:\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const order = await ordersApi.getOrderById('non-existent-id');\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error.status === 404) {\n    // Handle not found error\n    showNotFoundMessage();\n  } else if (error.status >= 400 && error.status < 500) {\n    // Handle client errors\n    showValidationError(error.message);\n  } else {\n    // Handle server or network errors\n    showServerError();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Related Components\n\n- [API Client](./api-client.md) - Base API client used by all API services\n- [Products API](./products-api.md) - API for product management\n- [Users API](./users-api.md) - API for user management")

